  "notes": [
   "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
   "Potentiometer is placed in one row (columns 13-15) in the card's order GND, SIG, VCC. The potentiometer is symmetric (GND=VCC), so I put 5V on the column 15 end and GND on the column 13 end. The image has the red wire at column 13 and the black at column 15, which is the same circuit with the pot flipped.",
   "In the image the A5 wire lands on the opposite half from the potentiometer's legs. I put it in the same column strip as the wiper (14) so the wiper reaches A5.",
   "Breadboard rows follow the catalogue naming (bank 't' = rows a-e). The lower rail pair is used: 'bn' is the ground rail (black line) and 'bp' is the 5V rail (red line). The rail hole numbers are approximate.",
   "The buzzer is polarised: pin 2 (+) is in column 26 and goes to A0 (the DAC output). Pin 1 (-) is in column 29 and goes to GND through the short black wire.",
   "The tutorial calls the buzzer-driving pin the DAC output; on the UNO R4 WiFi that is A0. A5 reads the potentiometer wiper."
  ]
